<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude"  xml:id="chapter-14-intro">
  <title>Week 14</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      At the end of this week you should be able to...
    </p>
    <objectives>
      <ul>
        <li>Read a program using overloading or varargs and explain what it does</li>
        <li>Read a program using exception handling and explain what it does</li>
        <li>Trace the flow of control during the execution of a program using exception handling</li>
        <li>Trace the flow of control during the execution of a program using file access</li>
        <li>Develop programs that use file I/O to provide data persistence across multiple executions</li>
        <li>Develop programs that can validate user input and handle runtime errors.</li>
      </ul>
    </objectives>
  </introduction>
  <xi:include href="sec-overloading.ptx"/>
  <xi:include href="sec-exception-handling.ptx"/>
  <xi:include href="sec-validation.ptx"/>
  <xi:include href="sec-file-io.ptx"/>
</chapter>
